(ServiceHub Backend: What Is in Place) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In one sentence) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This began as the starter structure for ServiceHub and now includes account, business,) Tj
T*
(service, staff, scheduling, and appointment flows. A scaffold is the foundation of a) Tj
T*
(project; the remaining feature modules are being built on it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What works today) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The server starts with `npm run dev`.) Tj
T*
(- `GET /api/v1/health` responds with `{ "status": "ok" }`.) Tj
T*
(- `POST /api/v1/auth/register` creates a user, a business, and an owner membership in one) Tj
T*
(transaction.) Tj
T*
(- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` checks the password and returns a 15-minute bearer access token.) Tj
T*
(- `GET /api/v1/auth/me` returns the signed-in user and their business memberships.) Tj
T*
(- Owners and admins can add existing accounts to a business with ADMIN, STAFF, or CUSTOMER) Tj
T*
(roles.) Tj
T*
(- `GET /api/v1/businesses/current` returns the active business selected from a verified) Tj
T*
(membership.) Tj
T*
(- Services can be listed, created, updated, and deactivated within the selected business.) Tj
T*
(- Staff records can be created, updated, deactivated, and assigned to services within the) Tj
T*
(selected business.) Tj
T*
(- Managers can replace weekly staff schedules; schedule times use the business time zone.) Tj
T*
(- Customers can view public service catalogs and available time slots, then book) Tj
T*
(appointments as guests or signed-in users.) Tj
T*
(- Business owners and staff can view tenant appointments; owners and admins can cancel or) Tj
T*
(complete them.) Tj
T*
(- Signed-in customers can review their own completed appointments.) Tj
T*
(- Booking and management changes create in-app notifications and business-scoped audit) Tj
T*
(records.) Tj
T*
(- Owners and admins can view dashboard summaries; platform administrators can review) Tj
T*
(platform totals and suspend or reactivate businesses.) Tj
T*
(- Passwords are stored using Node.js scrypt hashes; registration and login have a stricter) Tj
T*
(rate limit.) Tj
T*
(- The health endpoint has an automated test. The suite has not been rerun since the backend) Tj
T*
(features were added.) Tj
T*
(- Environment settings are checked with Zod when the app starts.) Tj
T*
(- Requests are logged, common security headers are set, CORS and JSON parsing are) Tj
T*
(configured, and API requests are rate limited.) Tj
T*
(- Errors go through one handler and use a consistent JSON shape: `{ "error": { "code":) Tj
T*
("...", "message": "..." } }`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(How the folders are organized) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `src/app.js` assembles Express middleware and routes. `src/server.js` starts the listening) Tj
T*
(server.) Tj
T*
(- `src/config/` validates settings. `src/middlewares/` includes authentication, tenant) Tj
T*
(membership, RBAC, request validation, rate limiting, and error handling.) Tj
T*
(- `src/modules/auth/` implements registration, login, and current-user profile.) Tj
T*
(`src/modules/businesses/` implements the current business route and membership lookup.) Tj
T*
(- `src/modules/services/`, `src/modules/staff/`, and `src/modules/schedules/` implement) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
